; tools/lispm-check's self-test of questions, run with --files selftest.lisp.
; A form that asks a bare "(Y or N)" fails at once, naming the question, and is
; answered No, though its value would match: the run must not wait out
; --timeout.  YES-OR-NO-P is not here: over TELNET it prints no prompt at all,
; only a beep, so it still waits out --timeout.  The self-test (run.sh) checks each verdict and its text,
; and the exit status 1.

; a bare question fails, and the listener answers the next case
(y-or-n-p "Selftest short question? ") => NIL
(check-selftest-square 8) => 64

; an error the case's condition-case does not see first: the listener's own
; "Enter the debugger" question after the error's message, answered No as before
(condition-bind ((error 'si:eval-abort-trivial-errors-handler)) (car 'selftest-symbol))
(check-selftest-square 10) => 100

; the question's words in a value, or in output with more after them, ask nothing
"Selftest? (Y or N) " => "Selftest? (Y or N) "
(progn (format t "Selftest? (Yes or No)~%") 'done) => DONE
(check-selftest-square 11) => 121
